# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=skyward (coverage label only --
# evening steers at no boss, the walk starts at the door same as any
# other), spec=rogue:assassination, style=flee, size=25, difficulty=heroic,
# view=820x1180,touch, save=carried (behaves as fresh per #273 -- the
# dev-server port is pid-derived so localStorage never actually carries
# across separate playbot invocations, so #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 is used to
# unlock the chain up to 25-heroic the same way every other "carried at
# heroic" cell in this job has).
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and direction.md's #6/#271 lines first. rogue:
# assassination has been played five times before (melee, auto, idle,
# wander) and never once under flee. flee at 25-heroic has been given to
# three specs so far (priest:discipline, shaman:restoration, hunter:
# marksmanship) and crossed THE VIGIL clean every single time at that
# size/difficulty -- a fourth style/spec pair at 25-heroic would be a fifth
# clean crossing in a row there, or the first stall at that tier. Rogue is
# also the one class on record with a clean THE VIGIL crossing under
# *melee* specifically (moveSpeed 178, the fastest in the roster, 2026-09-25)
# -- [[#6]]'s 2026-09-28 entry found that a slower class wiped under the
# same melee style and concluded raw speed, not the style, did the work in
# that one pass. flee moves the player away from danger rather than at the
# boss, so this is the first chance to see whether rogue's speed advantage
# still shows up under a style with the opposite steering term, or whether
# it was melee-specific all along.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

evening flee 260 6
state
shot after-evening
says
bill
